\": \"IEC 62052-11\"}, {\"notes\": \"Electricity metering equipment (AC) -Acceptance inspection -Part 31: Particular requirements for static meters for active energy (classes 0.2S, 0.5S, 1 and 2), Clause 5.4 to 5.10\", \"serv_code\": \"EM002\", \"serv_name\": \"Calibration/Testing of Energy Meters\", \"serv_method\": \"IEC 62058-31\"}, {\"notes\": \"specify\", \"serv_code\": \"OT001\", \"serv_name\": \"Others\", \"serv_method\": \"specify\"}, {\"notes\": \"Instrument Transformers-Part 1: Current Transformers\", \"serv_code\": \"ET001\", \"serv_name\": \"Testing of low current Energy Transformers\", \"serv_method\": \"IEC 60044-1\"}, {\"notes\": \"Instrument transformers -Part 1: General requirements Part 2: Additional requirements for current transformers\", \"serv_code\": \"ET002\", \"serv_name\": \"Testing of low current Energy Transformers\", \"serv_method\": \"IEC 61869-1&2\"}, {\"notes\": \"Circuit- breaker for overcurrent protection for house hold and similar installations\", \"serv_code\": \"CB001\", \"serv_name\": \"Testing of miniature breakers\", \"serv_method\": \"IEC 60898-2\"}]',1,6,1377,NULL,'127.0.0.1','2026-08-07 21:42:05','2026-08-07 21:42:05'),(17,15,15,'search_user_guide','{\"search\": \"Laboratory Configuration\"}','{\"found\": true, \"message\": \"4 relevant user-guide article(s) found.\", \"articles\": [{\"slug\": \"laboratory-configuration-overview\", \"title\": \"Laboratory Configuration Overview\", \"excerpt\": \"Laboratory Configuration Overview The Laboratory Configuration Module is the master-data area of the KPLC Meter Calibration Laboratory System. It is used to maintain standardized records that are reused throughout equipment registration, calibration requests, quotations, job cards, certificates and reports. Configuration Areas Laboratory Services – service codes, names, methods, notes and publication status. Equipment Types and Pricing – equipment type names and approved laboratory rates. Equipment Categories – controlled equipment classification groups. Equipment Manufacturers – approved manufacturers and contact details. Audit Trail – traceability of configuration changes. Opening the Module Sign in to the system. Open the More menu on the top navigation bar. Select Configuration. The buttons shown on the Configuration dashboard depend on the permissions assigned to the current user. Dashboard Information The dashboard shows summary cards for: Total laboratory services and active services. Total equipment pricing records. Total equipment categories. Total equipment manufacturers. Recently updated services and pricing records. Equipment records with incomplete configuration, where applicable.\", \"category\": \"laboratory-configuration\"}, {\"slug\": \"equipment-registration-configuration-integration\", \"title\": \"Equipment Registration and Configuration Integration\", \"excerpt\": \"Equipment Registration and Configuration Integration The Equipment module uses controlled values from Laboratory Configuration. This reduces duplicate names and ensures consistent reporting. Configuration Fields on Equipment Equipment Category – selected from active equipment categories. Manufacturer – selected from active approved manufacturers. Equipment Type / Pricing Category – selected from the equipment type pricing list. Published Base Rate – displayed from the selected equipment type. Creating Equipment Open Equipment. Click Add Equipment. Enter the equipment name, serial number and model. Select the configured category, manufacturer and equipment type. Confirm status and condition. Click Save Equipment. Editing Existing Equipment When editing an older record, an inactive category or manufacturer may still appear with the label Inactive – Current Selection. This allows the existing record to remain valid until a replacement selection is made. Configuration Completeness Equipment is considered fully configured when category, manufacturer and equipment type are all assigned. Equipment marked as configuration incomplete should be reviewed and updated through the Equipment edit page.\", \"category\": \"laboratory-configuration\"}, {\"slug\": \"laboratory-configuration-best-practices\", \"title\": \"Laboratory Configuration Best Practices\", \"excerpt\": \"Laboratory Configuration Best Practices Use Consistent Naming Use approved names for equipment types, categories and manufacturers. Avoid unnecessary abbreviations. Use unique, meaningful codes. Check for an existing record before creating a new one. Manage Status Carefully Use Inactive instead of deleting records that have already been used. Activate only services and manufacturers approved for current use. Review inactive records periodically. Manage Pricing Carefully Confirm rates before saving. Record pricing changes through an authorized user. Review the audit trail after significant changes. Ensure rates are entered as numeric values in Kenya shillings. Protect Data Integrity Do not create duplicate categories or manufacturers. Do not remove records linked to equipment. Complete missing configuration for legacy equipment. Use the equipment configuration completeness filter regularly. Well-maintained configuration improves document accuracy, search results, finance reporting and equipment traceability.\", \"category\": \"laboratory-configuration\"}, {\"slug\": \"laboratory-configuration-troubleshooting\", \"title\": \"Laboratory Configuration Troubleshooting and FAQ\", \"excerpt\": \"Laboratory Configuration Troubleshooting and FAQ ProblemLikely CauseRecommended Action Configuration menu is not visible The user lacks all configuration view permissions Ask an administrator to verify the assigned Spatie role and permissions User does not have the right permissions The requested route requires a permission not assigned to the user Confirm the route middleware and the user&apos;s effective permissions Add or Edit button is missing The user has view-only access Request the relevant create or edit permission where justified A service does not appear in operational forms The service is inactive Open the service record and activate it if approved A category or manufacturer cannot be deleted It is already linked to equipment Deactivate the record instead Equipment shows Configuration Incomplete Category, manufacturer or pricing type is missing Open the equipment edit page and complete all configuration fields A manufacturer is missing from the equipment form The manufacturer is inactive Activate it or select another approved manufacturer Pricing rate is incorrect The equipment type rate is outdated Ask an authorized user to update the pricing record Recent changes do not appear Application or permission cache may be stale Clear the relevant caches and sign in again Frequently Asked Questions Should an old configuration record be deleted? Normally no. Deactivate records that are already referenced by historical equipment or calibration data. Can a Lab Technician ed...\", \"category\": \"laboratory-configuration\"}], \"search_term\": \"Laboratory Configuration\"}',1,12,5711,NULL,'127.0.0.1','2026-08-07 21:42:46','2026-08-07 21:42:46'),(18,16,15,'get_equipment_pricing','[]','[{\"id\": 9, \"name\": \"1 Phase watt hour meter\", \"rate\": \"3000.00\"}, {\"id\": 11, \"name\": \"3 Phase CT&PT Connected watt hour Meter\", \"rate\": \"10000.00\"}, {\"id\": 10, \"name\": \"3 Phase Whole current watt hour Meter\", \"rate\": \"5000.00\"}, {\"id\": 2, \"name\": \"Ammeters\", \"rate\": \"5000.00\"}, {\"id\": 8, \"name\": \"Clamp on Meters\", \"rate\": \"5000.00\"}, {\"id\": 5, \"name\": \"CT Analyzer\", \"rate\": \"20000.00\"}, {\"id\": 6, \"name\": \"Current Transformer\", \"rate\": \"3000.00\"}, {\"id\": 7, \"name\": \"Frequency Meters\", \"rate\": \"5000.00\"}, {\"id\": 4, \"name\": \"Multimeters\", \"rate\": \"15000.00\"}, {\"id\": 12, \"name\": \"Ordinary low Voltage Transformer\", \"rate\": \"3000.00\"}, {\"id\": 15, \"name\": \"Panel Meter\", \"rate\": \"10000.00\"}, {\"id\": 13, \"name\": \"Resistance boxes\", \"rate\": \"15000.00\"}, {\"id\": 3, \"name\": \"Resistance(Meggers) Meters\", \"rate\": \"15000.00\"}, {\"id\": 1, \"name\": \"Voltmeters\", \"rate\": \"5000.00\"}, {\"id\": 14, \"name\": \"Watt Hour Meter Programming\", \"rate\": \"10000.00\"}]',1,10,855,NULL,'127.0.0.1','2026-08-09 14:23:11','2026-08-09 14:23:11');
